    // line 44
    vela_builder_add(v_out, VELA_STR("`fn f(x: Int) -> Int { return x + 1 }` defines a function; omitting `->` means it returns nothing. Parameter types are required. Functions returning values must return on every path. A parameter is read-only unless declared `x: mut T`. A call must say `f(mut x)`. No two mutable arguments may refer to the same variable or overlapping parts; arguments read while another argument mutates them can also be rejected. Compute a temporary first. Local mutability alone does not make a parameter mutable.\012", 500));
