    // line 60
    vela_builder_add(v_out, VELA_STR("`import text` loads `text.vl` beside the program, otherwise from std or declared dependencies. Call `text.trim(s)`; refer to `geometry.Point`. Imports do not open names. Declarations are private by default; `pub fn` and `pub type` export them. A public function's exposed types must also be public. A module may define `push`, `len`, or other built-in function names; the module's function wins in its own scope, and outside it is qualified. Import cycles and duplicate declarations are errors.\012", 495));
